{
  "_about": [
    "Editorial supplement, written for this reader and not taken from LSJ.",
    "",
    "Three jobs:",
    "  gloss    - a short meaning, used for the interlinear line and vocabulary",
    "             lists. These override the automatic extraction, which is",
    "             unreliable for the commonest words: LSJ marks Indo-European",
    "             cognates with the same <tr> tag it uses for translations, so",
    "             the scraper offers 'nar, ner-, nr' for ANER.",
    "  note     - a sentence of orientation shown in the word panel, mostly for",
    "             the people named in the dialogue.",
    "  suppress - Morpheus lemmas that are real dictionary headwords but wrong",
    "             here, so the reader skips them when choosing what to show:",
    "             DOKO -> DOKOS 'beam' rather than DOKEO 'seem'.",
    "",
    "The full LSJ entry is always shown underneath, unchanged."
  ],
